---@field config any Type-specific JSON. For path_drop: object with optional `filter_group` (PropertyGroupFilter shape — AND/OR tree of property predicates evaluated per record) and/or legacy `patterns` (list of regex strings) + `match_attribute_key` (string). When both are present a record is dropped if EITHER matches. Filter group example: `{"type":"AND","values":[{"type":"AND","values":[{"key":"service.name","operator":"exact","value":"api"}]}]}`. Every group in `filter_group` must contain at least one filter — empty groups never match, so the rule would never apply. For severity_sampling: object with `actions` per severity level and optional `always_keep`. For rate_limit: object with EITHER `logs_per_second` (integer 1–1000000, optional `burst_logs` integer ≥ logs_per_second, max 10000000) OR `kb_per_second` (integer 1–1000000 = 1 GB/s, optional `burst_kb` integer ≥ kb_per_second, max 10000000) — not both. Plus optional `filter_group` to narrow which logs the cap applies to. KB-mode charges each log its own uncompressed byte size, matching how billing measures ingested bytes.

