---@class posthog.logs.LogPattern
---@field pattern string Log template with variable tokens masked, e.g. "Connected to <ip> in <num>ms". Body mining masks <timestamp>, <uuid>, <ip>, <hex>, <num>, plus <*> for word positions Drain found to vary. Stored patterns use the ingestion vocabulary instead: <N>, <TIMESTAMP>, <KLOGTIME>, <UUID>, <IP>, <HOST>, <HEX>, <ID>, <EMAIL>, <JSON_ARRAY>, and <JSON:keys> for a JSON body reduced to its key set.
---@field count number Occurrences of this pattern within the sample. When `sampled` is true this is a sample count, not the full-window total — prefer `estimated_count` for display.
---@field estimated_count number Estimated occurrences across the full window, extrapolated from the sample (`count / scanned_count * total_count`). Equals `count` when the window was not sampled.
---@field volume_share_pct number Share of the log volume this pattern represents (0–100). Measured over the sample when `sampled` is true, over every matching row otherwise.
---@field error_count number Occurrences at severity "error" or "fatal". A sample count when `sampled` is true, so prefer `estimated_error_count` for display.
---@field estimated_error_count number Estimated error/fatal occurrences across the full window, extrapolated from the sample. Equals `error_count` when the window was not sampled.
---@field first_seen string ISO 8601 timestamp of the earliest occurrence. Taken from the sample when `sampled` is true, from every matching row otherwise.
---@field last_seen string ISO 8601 timestamp of the latest occurrence. Taken from the sample when `sampled` is true, from every matching row otherwise.
---@field examples posthog.logs.LogPatternExamplesList Up to 10 distinct sampled log lines that produced this pattern, with severity, service, and timestamp for display.
---@field services posthog.logs.LogPatternServicesList Up to 4 distinct service names this pattern was observed in.
---@field sparkline posthog.logs.LogPatternSparklineList Occurrences per time bucket, aligned index-for-index with the response's `sparkline_buckets`. When `sampled` is true these are extrapolated like `estimated_count` and show the volume shape over the window rather than exact tallies. Otherwise they are exact per-bucket counts.
---@field severity_counts posthog.logs.LogPatternSeverityCountsMap Occurrences keyed by lowercased severity ("trace" through "fatal"). Never extrapolated, because severity dominance is a proportion that scaling would not change. Sample counts when `sampled` is true, counts over every matching row otherwise.
---@field match_regex string|distilled.Null RE2-safe regex over raw log bodies that matches lines of this pattern, compiled from the template and validated against the raw bodies of the pattern's own sampled rows before being offered. Null when the template lacks literal content or validation failed. Never trust an unvalidated predicate. Use with the message/regex log property filter.
---@field match_literal string|distilled.Null Longest literal run in the template, for plain-text (icontains) filtering when `match_regex` is null. Null when the template has no usable literal content.
---@field match_patterns? posthog.logs.LogPatternMatchPatternsList Exact canonical members of a stored-pattern group. Filter pattern IN these values AND pattern_version equals this group's version. Empty for body mining.
---@field pattern_version? number|distilled.Null Version required by match_patterns. Null for body mining.

---@class posthog.logs.LogPatternDiffEntry
---@field masked_example string The template with variable parts masked.
---@field services posthog.logs.LogPatternDiffEntryServicesList Up to 4 services with this pattern.
---@field first_seen_ever string|distilled.Null Earliest 5-minute bucket (UTC) with this pattern, up to 14 days back. Null on body mining.
---@field classification posthog.logs.LogPatternDiffEntryClassificationEnum "new": appears only in the current window and clears the novelty floor (at least ~1% volume share, or any error/fatal occurrences). "rate_shift": present in both windows with the per-second rate changed by at least 2x either way, backed by enough samples on both sides to trust the estimates. "gone": cleared the floor in the baseline but absent from the current window. "unchanged" means "no confident claim", not "provably identical" — sampled mining cannot prove a below-floor template is genuinely new or gone. * `new` - new * `rate_shift` - rate_shift * `gone` - gone * `unchanged` - unchanged
---@field rate_ratio number|distilled.Null Current-window rate divided by baseline rate, both normalized per second so windows of different lengths compare fairly. 4.0 means 4x faster now; 0.25 means quartered. Null when the pattern is missing from either window.
---@field pattern posthog.logs.LogPattern The mined pattern with full stats. Taken from the current window, or from the baseline window for "gone" entries. When template wobble split one message across several near-identical templates, this is the highest-volume representative and the entry's classification reflects their combined counts.
---@field baseline_estimated_count number|distilled.Null Estimated occurrences across the baseline window (extrapolated like `estimated_count`). Null when the pattern was not seen in the baseline sample.
---@field baseline_volume_share_pct number|distilled.Null Share of the baseline sample this pattern represented (0-100). Null when absent from the baseline.

---* `new` - new
---* `rate_shift` - rate_shift
---* `gone` - gone
---* `unchanged` - unchanged
---@alias posthog.logs.LogPatternDiffEntryClassificationEnum "new"|"rate_shift"|"gone"|"unchanged"

---Up to 4 services with this pattern.
---@alias posthog.logs.LogPatternDiffEntryServicesList string[]

