---@class posthog.logs.LogsAlertConfiguration
---@field id? string Unique identifier for this alert.
---@field name? string Human-readable name for this alert. Defaults to 'Untitled alert' on create when omitted.
---@field enabled? boolean Whether the alert is actively being evaluated. Disabling resets the state to not_firing.
---@field filters? posthog.logs.LogsAlertFilters Filter criteria — subset of LogsViewerFilters. Must contain at least one of: severityLevels (list of severity strings), serviceNames (list of service name strings), or filterGroup (property filter group object). May be empty on draft alerts (enabled=false).
---@field threshold_count? number Number of matching log entries that constitutes a threshold breach within the evaluation window. Defaults to 100. Use 0 with the 'above' operator to fire on any matching log.
---@field threshold_operator? posthog.logs.LogsAlertConfigurationThresholdOperatorEnum Whether the alert fires when the count is above or below the threshold. * `above` - Above * `below` - Below
---@field window_minutes? number Time window in minutes over which log entries are counted. Allowed values: 5, 10, 15, 30, 60.
---@field check_interval_minutes? number How often the alert is evaluated, in minutes. Server-managed.
---@field state? posthog.logs.LogsAlertConfigurationStateEnum Current alert state: not_firing, firing, pending_resolve, errored, or snoozed. Server-managed. * `not_firing` - Not firing * `firing` - Firing * `pending_resolve` - Pending resolve * `errored` - Errored * `snoozed` - Snoozed * `broken` - Broken
---@field evaluation_periods? number Total number of check periods in the sliding evaluation window for firing (M in N-of-M).
---@field datapoints_to_alarm? number How many periods within the evaluation window must breach the threshold to fire (N in N-of-M).
---@field cooldown_minutes? number Minimum minutes between notifications. The alert notifies once when it starts firing and once when it resolves. It does not notify again on each check while it stays firing. A fire or resolve notification inside the cooldown is skipped. Cooldown does not apply to PagerDuty incidents. 0 means no minimum.
---@field schedule_restriction? posthog.logs.AlertScheduleRestriction|distilled.Null Blocked local time windows when the alert must not run. Times use the project timezone. Null disables quiet hours.
---@field snooze_until? string|distilled.Null ISO 8601 timestamp until which the alert is snoozed. Set to null to unsnooze.
---@field next_check_at? string|distilled.Null When the next evaluation is scheduled. Server-managed.
---@field last_notified_at? string|distilled.Null When the last notification was sent. Server-managed.
---@field last_checked_at? string|distilled.Null When the alert was last evaluated. Server-managed.
---@field consecutive_failures? number Number of consecutive evaluation failures. Resets on success. Server-managed.
---@field last_error_message? string|distilled.Null Error message from the most recent errored check, or null if the alert's most recent check was successful. Sourced from LogsAlertEvent without denormalization so retention-aware cleanup rules stay the only source of truth. For an alert the alerts platform evaluates, sourced from the platform's check history.
---@field state_timeline? posthog.logs.LogsAlertConfigurationStateTimelineList Continuous state intervals over the last 24h, ordered oldest-first. Each interval covers a span during which (state, enabled) was constant. Derived from LogsAlertEvent rows walked in chronological order; consecutive identical intervals are collapsed. For an alert the alerts platform evaluates, state changes come from the platform's check history instead. Drives the 'Last 24h' status bar on the alert list.
---@field destination_types? posthog.logs.LogsAlertConfigurationDestinationTypesList Notification destination types configured for this alert — e.g. 'slack', 'webhook'. Empty list means no notifications will fire. One or more destinations should be added after creating an alert.
---@field grouping? posthog.logs.LogsAlertGrouping How the alert splits its results into instances. Mode single keeps one instance for the whole alert. Mode by_result_labels with keys service_name and/or severity_text keeps one instance per service or severity, each firing and resolving on its own, and needs threshold_operator above. Only an alert the alerts platform evaluates can group. Any other alert reads as single and rejects a different value. Omit it on update to keep the current grouping. Changing the keys deletes the existing instances and closes their notification threads without a message.
---@field platform_owned boolean Whether the alerts platform evaluates this alert and sends its notifications. Only such an alert can set a grouping other than single.
---@field first_enabled_at? string|distilled.Null When the alert was first enabled. Null means the alert is still in draft state.
---@field created_at? string When the alert was created.
---@field created_by? posthog.logs.UserBasic|distilled.Null
---@field updated_at? string|distilled.Null When the alert was last modified.

