---@class posthog.logs.LogsSeriesBandBucket
---@field time string Start of the display bucket (UTC).
---@field observed number Log count observed in this bucket.
---@field lower number|distilled.Null Lower edge of the calibrated count range targeting 99% marginal bucket coverage under stable traffic. Null without four complete preceding weeks.
---@field upper number|distilled.Null Upper edge of the calibrated count range targeting 99% marginal bucket coverage under stable traffic. Null without four complete preceding weeks.
---@field verdict posthog.logs.LogsSeriesBandVerdictEnum|distilled.Null Where the observed count sits against the band: above when it exceeds upper, below when it falls under lower. Null while it sits inside the band, or while the band is not ready. An out-of-range bucket is not a confirmed incident or an alert. * `above` - Above the band * `below` - Below the band

---@class posthog.logs.LogsSeriesBandSeries
---@field namespace string Namespace of the emitting resource; empty when the logs carry none.
---@field environment string Deployment environment of the emitting resource; empty when the logs carry none.
---@field severity string Lowercased log severity of this series (for example info, error).
---@field total_count number Total observed log count over the window. Series are ordered by this, descending.
---@field baseline_weeks number Full weeks of history behind the band, 0 to 5. Four complete weeks are required: at least two for fitting and two separate weeks for calibration.
---@field history_start string Start of sustained traffic inside the fetched lookback: the first bucket followed by a week with enough non-empty buckets. A stray earlier row does not move it. The window start when no traffic is sustained yet.
---@field band_ready_at string|distilled.Null Earliest end of a rolling window of this length with four complete preceding weeks. Null when the band is ready. A fixed historical window does not gain history by waiting. Check the buckets' lower and upper values to determine whether a band is present.
---@field interval_minutes number Grain of this series' buckets, in minutes. Equals the response interval_minutes unless the series was too sparse at that grain and was coarsened to the next rung it is dense enough to read at.
---@field coarsened_reason posthog.logs.CoarsenedReasonEnum|distilled.Null Why this series was too thin to read at the requested grain, or null when it was not. sparse: fewer than 20% of its buckets held any records. quiet: its non-empty buckets averaged under 5 records. A series that fails every rung is returned at the coarsest one. A series that a coarser rung has no rows for, or that the request's time budget cannot refetch, keeps the requested grain and still carries its reason. * `sparse` - sparse * `quiet` - quiet
---@field buckets posthog.logs.LogsSeriesBandSeriesBucketsList One entry per display bucket across the window at this series' interval_minutes, oldest first, zero-filled. A coarsened series' window is snapped to its grain, so it can end short of window_end.

---One entry per display bucket across the window at this series' interval_minutes, oldest first, zero-filled. A coarsened series' window is snapped to its grain, so it can end short of window_end.
---@alias posthog.logs.LogsSeriesBandSeriesBucketsList posthog.logs.LogsSeriesBandBucket[]

---* `above` - Above the band
---* `below` - Below the band
---@alias posthog.logs.LogsSeriesBandVerdictEnum "above"|"below"

