---@class posthog.logs.UpdateLogsRetentionRuleRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field id string A UUID string identifying this logs retention rule.
---@field name string User-visible label for this rule.
---@field enabled? boolean When false, the rule is ignored by ingestion and listing UIs that show active rules only.
---@field priority? number|distilled.Null Lower numbers are evaluated first; the first matching rule wins. Omit to append after existing rules.
---@field config any Retention rule JSON. Required keys: `retention_days` (integer — how long matching logs are kept; must be a tier the organization is entitled to, same as the team-wide Logs retention setting) and `filter_group` (PropertyGroupFilter shape — an AND/OR tree of property predicates evaluated per record to decide which logs this rule matches). Example: `{"retention_days":30,"filter_group":{"type":"AND","values":[{"type":"AND","values":[{"key":"service.name","operator":"exact","value":"api"}]}]}}`. Logs matching no enabled rule keep the environment's default retention.

---@class posthog.logs.UpdateLogsRetentionRulesPartialRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
